        <mxCell id="lgExtText" value="«extends» — the source extends the configuration of the target" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="140" y="978" width="290" height="24" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rules" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Dependencies point downwards: the two applications depend on the packages, and a package never imports from an application.&lt;br&gt;2. No route module of apps/api imports another route module; cross-module data flows through the Prisma schema.&lt;br&gt;3. Arrows drawn from the apps group apply to both apps/web and apps/api. eslint-config is applied to every workspace (the arrows from packages/ui and packages/shared-type are omitted for readability).&lt;br&gt;4. Python AI microservices (id-verification, cv-matching, ai-moderation backed by Ollama) reside in ai-services/ and communicate with apps/api via HTTP REST, independent of the TypeScript pnpm workspaces." style="shape=note;size=16;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=12;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="460" y="900" width="1080" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

